Article 3 (Items of Expenditure and Calculation Methods)
(1) The items of expenditure forming the basis for determining admission screening fees shall be as follows: [Amended on August 30, 2018.]
1. Allowances: The following expenses paid to persons performing duties related to admission screening. In such cases, allowances shall not be paid for purposes other than reimbursement of actual expenses, such as performance bonuses:
(a) Allowances for preparing questions: Expenses incurred in preparing questions for essay examinations, practical examinations, etc.;
(b) Allowances for examination supervision: Expenses incurred in supervising essay examinations, practical examinations, etc.;
(c) Allowances for evaluation: Expenses incurred in grading and evaluating documents, essay examinations, practical examinations, etc.;
(d) Allowances for preparation and administration: Expenses incurred in preparing and conducting admission screening, including interviews, essay examinations, and practical examinations;
(e) Allowances for admission screening information: Expenses incurred in publicizing admission screening, including holding information sessions and fairs;
(f) Meeting allowances: Expenses incurred in attending meetings on admission screening convened by a university.
2. Expenses: The following expenses, other than allowances, incurred in performing duties related to admission screening:
(a) Publicity expenses: Expenses incurred in holding information sessions, participating in fairs, and providing promotional materials concerning admission or other admission screening information. In such cases, publicity expenses shall not be used to produce or purchase promotional items;
(b) Meeting expenses: Expenses incurred in holding meetings related to admission screening;
(c) Fees for entrusting duties: Expenses incurred in entrusting a third party with part of the duties related to admission screening;
(d) Printing expenses: Expenses incurred in producing printed materials related to admission screening, including application forms, admission guidelines, and guidebooks;
(e) Expenses for purchasing materials: Expenses incurred in purchasing materials for the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(f) Expenses for consumables: Expenses incurred in purchasing consumables for the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(g) Public utility charges: Expenses such as electricity, water, communications, heating, and postage charges arising from the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(h) Meal expenses: Meal expenses arising from the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(i) Travel expenses: Expenses for business trips arising from the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(j) Parking fees: Parking fees arising from the performance of duties related to admission screening;
(k) Facility use fees: Expenses for using facilities in the performance of duties related to admission screening.
