(2) Allowances and expenses under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be calculated by the following methods. Specific calculation methods, including unit payment rates, shall be determined following deliberation by the admission screening deliberative body of each university, such as its University Admission Screening Management Committee: [Newly inserted on August 30, 2018.]
1. Allowances shall be calculated by predicting the number of applicants for each type of screening, determining the number of persons to be engaged and the hours to be worked, etc., and multiplying these by the payment rates of the relevant university.
2. Expenses shall be calculated by predicting the number of applicants for each type of screening, determining the number of persons to be engaged, hours to be worked, quantities, areas, frequencies, etc., and multiplying these by the payment rates of the relevant university.
(3) Publicity expenses under paragraph (1) 2 (a) shall not exceed the following respective limits: [Amended on August 30, 2018.]
1. Universities with an admission quota of fewer than 1,300 students: 35 percent of the total expenditure from admission screening fees;
2. Universities with an admission quota of at least 1,300 but fewer than 2,500 students: 25 percent of the total expenditure from admission screening fees;
3. Universities with an admission quota of at least 2,500 students: 15 percent of the total expenditure from admission screening fees.
